<title>SOUTH AFRICA: COATES RENEWS CAUTIONARY ON SUSPENDED TALKS.</title>
<headline>COATES RENEWS CAUTIONARY ON SUSPENDED TALKS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coates Brothers (South Africa) Ltd on Thursday renewed a cautionary published on May 30 in which it said that talks between itself and The Valspar Corp had been temporarily suspended.</p>
<p>It said in that announcement that the talks related to the sale of Coates' can coatings division to Valspar. It said then that the negotiations would resume during August.</p>
<p>Shareholders were advised to exercise caution in their share dealings.</p>
<p>A further announcement would be made when the talks recommenced, Coates said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
